// A builtin operation on the value carrier's REPRESENTATION is refused.
// The carrier's C storage is a long long array, so every one of these used
// to compile with exit 0 and a garbage answer (at most a c2mir warning):
// `x + 1` was pointer arithmetic on the storage, `x < y` an address compare,
// `int a = x` the storage address, and `if (f)` was always taken — the
// decayed address is never null — even for a false or null value. A plain
// class operand is a c2mir error already; the carrier's representation hid
// it. The carrier converts EXPLICITLY (as_integer / as_real / as_boolean) or
// to text (c_str, and the `const char *` coercion). The expected lines are
// gcc's wording for a class that lacks the operator or conversion (madc
// spells int as its int32_t).
int take(int v) { return v; }
int give() { var r = 7; return r; }
int main()
{
	var x = 5;
	var y = 6;
	var f = false;
	int s = 0;
	s = x + 1;
	if (x < y) s = 2;
	x -= 1;
	int a = x;
	int b = 0;
	b = x;
	int c = take(x);
	if (f) s = 3;
	println("{} {} {} {} {}", s, a, b, c, give());
	return 0;
}
